  "security_implications": "valid_tracking_q controls which sideload key slots are considered valid. Erroneous set or clear caused by conflicting slot_sel/slot_clr, missing protocol definition, or a bit flip could allow use of uninitialized, stale, or zeroized keys, violating confidentiality and integrity. The clear priority over set may mask an intended set operation, leading to denial of service or forced use of a default/weak key. As part of the key access control mechanism, the correctness and fault robustness of this tracking vector are critical.",
